export anchor ConcertStageStyle:
    number: 328
    screen: MusicPlayer
    name: Concert stage
    idea: The player is a live stage seen from the crowd, with light beams falling from a truss, the song title lit in a spotlight, a crowd silhouette along the front and the queue taped down as a hand set list.
    base: dark
    palette:
        backdrop: #0b0912, the page, the stage and the style sheet
        floor: #15121d, the control barrier, the set list card and the passes
        truss: #2f2a3a, the truss bar, borders and dividers
        houseLight: #f7f3ec, titles and body text
        haze: #b8b0c4, artists, times and labels
        spot: #ffcf5a, the spotlight pool, the pause button, the current set list row and focus
        onSpot: #1f1500, text on spot
        beamViolet: #8a5cff, decorative beams only, never behind text
        tape: #d8c48e, gaffer tape on the set list and the strap edge of each pass
    type:
        Titles use a condensed stack, Avenir Next Condensed, Arial Narrow,
        Roboto Condensed, Helvetica Neue, Arial, in caps at 800. Body uses
        Helvetica Neue and Arial at 15px. The title is clamp 52 to 104px
        with 0.92 line height, set list titles 26px, the lyric on screen
        32px at 600, pass names 22px, and caps labels 12px at 700 with
        0.24em tracking.
    layout:
        A stage over a control barrier, with a set list column on the
        right. The stage is about 560px tall, with a hatched truss bar and
        six glowing lamps across the top, five light beams in warm white
        and violet fanning down, a soft amber pool in the centre, then the
        caps line Brightwork Sound, On stage now, the huge condensed title,
        and the artist with Low Tide. A black crowd silhouette with some
        raised hands runs along the bottom edge. The barrier under the
        stage holds round outlined buttons with caps words beneath,
        Shuffle, Prev, a larger spot yellow Pause, Next, Repeat and Liked
        with a filled heart, then a thick progress rail with elapsed and
        total time, and Crowd volume as ten rising bars with seven lit and
        70%. The right column holds a slightly tilted dark card held by two
        tape strips, titled Tonight's set, with Harbour Lights first on a
        spot yellow band with a play arrow and Now, then the five queued
        songs in big condensed caps with numbers and times. A black screen
        band shows Lyrics on screen with the current line large behind a
        play arrow and the next line smaller. Backstage shows the three
        playlists as passes with a tape strap edge and a punched slot,
        plus caps links for Albums, Artists and Podcasts. Below 1060px the
        set list moves under the barrier, and below 560px everything
        stacks.
    spacing: An 8px unit. A tall stage, 20 to 32px section padding and 10px set list rows.
    density: Low on the stage, medium on the set list and the passes.
    corners: Square stage, barrier and set list, 4px passes, round transport buttons.
    borders: The truss bar with lamps across the top, 1px truss rules elsewhere, tape strips instead of a frame on the set list.
    shadows: None on boxes. Light does the work, an amber pool behind the title and beams at 18 to 20 percent.
    icons:
        Solid glyphs inside round outlined buttons with caps words below.
        Liked is a filled heart in a spot ring with the word Liked. The set
        list marks the current song with a play arrow and the word Now.
    focus: A 3px spot outline offset 3px.
    tone: Live show words, such as On stage now, Tonight's set, Lyrics on screen, Backstage and Crowd volume.
